==German==

===Etymology===
Compound of {{compound|hacken|Fleisch|lang=de}} (“hacked meat”).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhakˌflaɪ̯ʃ/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Hackfleischs|gen2=Hackfleisches|-}}

# [[mince]]d [[meat]]
#: ''Frikadellen sind aus '''Hackfleisch'''.''
#:: Meatballs are made from '''minced meat.'''.''
# {{context|figurative|informal|lang=de}} the [[victim]] of a [[beating]] or a harsh [[reprehension]]
#: ''Aus dem mach ich '''Hackfleisch'''!''
#:: (''literally:'') I'll make him into minced meat!
#: ''Wenn der Direktor das mitkriegt, bist du '''Hackfleisch'''.''
#:: (''literally:'') If the principal finds out about that, you'll be minced meat.

